A truck R of mass $9400\text{ kg}$ moves with constant acceleration in a straight line down a slope, as illustrated in Fig. 3.1.

{{figure:figure_3_1.png}}

At point A the speed of the truck is $13\text{ m s}^{-1}$ and at point B the speed of the truck is $22\text{ m s}^{-1}$. A and B are a distance of $180\text{ m}$ apart.
